# Web Remote Manager PRO - License

Web Remote Manager PRO ("WRM") is source-available. You may use it under either of the two licenses below, whichever fits what you do:

1. PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 - for any noncommercial purpose, including sharing the software and modified versions for noncommercial purposes.
2. PolyForm Internal Use License 1.0.0 - for the internal business operations of you and your company, including for-profit companies. This license does not allow distributing the software.

Anything neither license allows requires a separate written commercial license from the copyright holder (see COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md).

These terms apply to every version of WRM published in this repository, including releases published before these terms were added.

## Licensor's clarifications

These clarifications are part of the licensor's terms. They explain how the licensor applies the licenses above and grant permission where they say something is allowed. They never take away rights that the licenses give you.

1. Using WRM as a work tool is internal business use. Your employees and contractors may use WRM to do your company's work on any number of servers and computers, including paid work for your own customers (for example, managing your customers' servers). They may invite customers or partners into a shared session or call while working with them. This is allowed free of charge as long as your customers pay for your work and not for WRM.

2. The following are not internal business use. Unless the Noncommercial license allows them (for example, a charity offering WRM to others free of charge), they require a commercial license:
   a. providing WRM, original or modified, to third parties as a hosted, managed or cloud service (SaaS), including giving third parties their own accounts on a WRM installation that you run for them;
   b. charging anyone, directly or indirectly, for access to or use of WRM, or offering access to WRM as a product or as part of a paid product, plan or subscription;
   c. selling, reselling, renting, leasing, sublicensing or white-labelling WRM;
   d. bundling WRM with, or including WRM or code from it in, a product, appliance or service that you distribute or offer to others;
   e. distributing WRM or modified versions of it for a commercial purpose.

3. If you are not sure whether your use is allowed, ask the licensor before you start (see COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md).

